## Audit: the orchestration surface

Surface is `packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/lib/` — `quality-gates.js` (1247), `tools.js` (3736), `state.js` (1596), `scheduler.js` (834). Provenance: *adopted `@nanmicoder/dsh-agent-teams` 0.1.14 body + backported 0.1.16-rc.3 deltas*, with local patches carried as `mpd-delta` regions in `lib/mpd-deltas.js`, re-applied by `scripts/patch-agent-teams-fixes.mjs`.

**Root cause of the routing defect (T-93), `quality-gates.js:807`:**

```js
function schedulableAssignee(preferred, team, forbidden) {
  if (preferred !== undefined && preferred !== CAPTAIN_ASSIGNEE && preferred !== forbidden) {
    const live = team.members.find(m => m.name === preferred && m.status !== 'removed')
    if (live !== undefined) return live.name
  }
  return team.members.find(m => m.status !== 'removed' && m.name !== CAPTAIN_ASSIGNEE && m.name !== forbidden)?.name
}
```

It filters on status and the captain — **it never reads `member.toolDeny`**. Two leak paths:

1. `:884` `const implementer = schedulableAssignee(source?.assignee, team)` — the auto-generated repair is `kind: 'repair'`, and `:15` `WRITE_KINDS = ['implementation','repair']`, so it is unambiguously a write task assigned with no capability test.
2. The `:813` fallback returns the **first non-removed, non-captain member in roster order** — in the mpd roster that is **Architect**, a read-only seat holding the seven write-tool denials. The fallback deterministically routes a write-kind repair to a seat that cannot execute it.

**Why the existing guard misses it:** `mpd-deltas.js` already has `taskCapabilityNeed` (repair ⇒ needs writes), `taskCapabilityGap` (reads `toolDeny`), and `nextCapableTask` — but it documents that *"the member's OWN task always wins: an explicit assignment is the captain's decision, so it is dispatched even to a restricted member."* An auto-generated repair carries `assignee: <name>`, so it **is** an explicit assignment and the guard stands down by design. The defect is the *assignment*, not the dispatch. Fix shape (T-93's own acceptance): make `schedulableAssignee` capability-aware, preferring the reviewed artifact's author when capable, else the first capable writer — with `tools.js:3464` (`new Set(memberEntry?.toolDeny ?? [])`, `ARTIFACT_WRITE_NAMES`) as the "way the spawn surface does" reference.

## The finding that needs your call

**Upstream has the identical unfixed function.** `dsh-agent-teams src/quality-gates.ts:552` carries the same three filters and no `toolDeny` read (upstream is at `0.1.16-rc.3`).

So *"align the bundle with upstream"* and *"implement the routing change"* are **not the same operation** — aligning cannot produce this routing change, because upstream is the **origin** of the defect. If the intent was "adopt upstream's routing change," there is nothing to adopt; it must be authored locally as an mpd delta + self-fix test.

